1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Wright (Wraight) was born in Cranbrook, Kent, England and emigrated to New Zealand aboard the Martha Ridgway in November 1840.   Landing in Petone, Wellington, the family spent two years living in the camp th
2 CONC ere before boarding the Bright Planet and sailing to Lyttelton in 1842   He worked as a shore whaler at Oashore and eventually became the manager of the station.   He purchased 50 acres of land at Whakamoa and then went into partn
2 CONC ership with William Lucas at L:ands End.   He was a big man, fiery of temper and a gambler and gave his wife quite a hard time.   He died aged 78 and had a huge funeral attended by most of the population  who gathered to say goodb
2 CONC ye the "The Baron of Whakamoa."
