2 DATE 19 AUG 1975
2 ADDR
3 CITY Leppington
3 STAE NSW
3 CTRY Australia
1 OCCU Railwayman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Walter Thomas Tickner Death Notice Sydney Morning Herald 18 August 1975
2 CONT
2 CONT August 17 1975 (suddenly) late of Somerset Street Minto loved husband of Ada beloved father of Edward, Leslie (deceased) Bevan, Esma, Bertha and Ray fond father-in-law of Helen, Angela (Deceased) Andrew, Gordon and Alla, loved gra
2 CONC ndfather and great-grandfather of their children, also fond brother of Gordon (Moss Vale). For funeral arrangements see Tuesday's Herald
2 CONT
2 CONT Tickner - The relatives and friends of the late Walter Thomas Tickner of Somerset Street Minto are respectfully invited to attend his funeral to leave St James Church of England Redfern Street Minto this day (Tuesday) August 19 on
2 CONC  conclusion of service commencing at 11am for the Forest Lawn Memorial Garden Hume Highway Leppington
2 CONT
2 CONT 60th WEDDING  ANNIVERSARY  OF WALTER THOMAS  AND  ADA  ELIZA  TICKNER  ( NEE CAUNT )
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a gathering  of the clan At Audley National Park, Sutherland on September 2nd, to  celebrate the 60th wedding  anniversary  of Walter and Ada Tickner  of  Minto. Their well-wishes included their four serviving  children,
2 CONC 21 grandchildren, 33 great grandchildren  their  foster  son  Ray  Kerr  and  Mr Tickner's only living  brother Gordon Tickner and his wife  from  Moss  Vale On their anniversary, which fell  on September 1, the couple  spent an e
2 CONC xciting day  opening  up congradulatory  telegrames from Queens Elizabeth, the Prime  Minister Mr Whitlam, the Govennor  Sir  Roden  Cutler and from relatives and friends. Mr and Mrs Tickner were married at the small town of Grong
2 CONC  Grong ( near Narrandera ) and moved to Minto in 1920. Came from Campbelltown  local paper in  September 1974 I still have the artical from 1974
