1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NSW Births Deaths & Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth of Jonathon and his siblings
2 CONT
2 CONT NB No Registration found for the 1st child, Rebecca born in Sydney 3rd July 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT Registration Number  Last Name  Given Name(s)  Father's Given Name(s)  Mother's Given Name(s)  District 
2 CONT
2 CONT V1847673 55/1847      WILLIS  SARAH      TIMOTHY  SARAH     
2 CONT
2 CONT V18491745 55/1849    WILLIS  WILLIAM    TIMOTHY  SARAH 
2 CONT
2 CONT V185118 60/1851         WILLIS  EMMA        TIMOTHY  SARAH  
2 CONT
2 CONT V18542270 56/1854    WILLIS  GEORGE  TIMOTHY  SARAH  
2 CONT
2 CONT 4093/1856                     WILLIS  CHARLES  TIMOTHY  SARAH  CAMDEN
2 CONT
2 CONT 6152/1859   WILLIS  JOHN T                        TIMOTHY  SARAH  CAMDEN     
2 CONT
2 CONT 6264/1861  WILLIS  JAMES J  TIMOTHY  SARAH  CAMDEN 
2 CONT
2 CONT  6509/1863                     WILLIS  JONATHAN  TIMOTHY  SARAH  CAMDEN  
2 CONT
2 CONT 5835/1864      WILLIS  HENRY    TIMOTHY  SARAH  BERRIMA
2 CONT
2 CONT 6560/1868   WILLIS  ELIZABETH A  TIMOTHY  SARAH  BERRIMA 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7254/1871  WILLIS  SAMUEL  TIMOTHY  SARAH  BERRIMA    
2 CONT
2 CONT From the "Willis Family History" prepared by Dell Bungay (nee Willis), Wagga Wagga 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Jonathon Willis was the ninth child and sixth son of Timothy and Sarah. He was born at Camden on 16th December, 1862, and moved with his family to Bowral in 1864. In his early days he followed in his father's  footsteps by being 
2 CONC a brickmaker. On 23 July 1884, at the age of 21 years, Jonathon married Emily Tickner aged 20 years from Moss Vale, at North Goulburn. Emily was the daughter of Henry and Martha Tickner (nee Rideout) and she was born at Camden on 
2 CONC 26 May, 1864. Jonathon and Emily had seven children. Their eldest son, Ubert Victor, was born on 4 December, 1885, then Henry Nelson was born in 1887. He died at Bowral on 2 April, 1897. Charles Percival was born on 19 july 1890, 
2 CONC joseph Henry on 18 january 1893 and Camden Kell on 22 December 1895. Their only daughter Mary May was born on 25 April, 1898, followed by Jack Jeffreee on 19 Januray 1905. Jonathon built his homestead "Rookwood", so named after th
2 CONC e Rook, a blckbird of the crow family commonly found in Europe and Asia. The homestead was surrounded by trees occupied by crows. This was on Kangaloon Road, Bowral, on a very large estate which included private slaughter yards an
2 CONC d several brick kilns. He later sold part of the estate to Bowral Golf Club to enable it to lay out their second nine holes. His calling as a brickmaker continued until 1909 when he went into the butchery trade, and conducted a su
2 CONC ccessful business in Bowral until 1922 when he retired. Jonathon was a keen rifleman and a member of the Bowral volunteers. Like most of his family he was fond of music, and at the age of 20, in 1883 was a founding member of the o
2 CONC riginal Bowral Band, together with his brothers, charles (270, John (25) Henry (19) and a nephew Fred Pain (15). He was still a member in 1899, when he retired from the Band. Jonathon was a noted cornettist. Jonathon's homestead h
2 CONC ad a music room and all their children learnt to play musical instruments. On 23rd July, 1907 Jonathon was appointed a member of the Council of the Municipality of Bowral by proclamation signed by Sir Harry Rawson, then Govenor of
2 CONC  NSW. Jonathon named his youngest son, Jack Jeffress, to continue his father'sdesire to keep the Jeffress connection with the Australian Sugar Company for prosperity. Timothy had named his 5th son, James Jeffress for the same reas
2 CONC on. (The Jeffress connection has been continued into the 6th generation by a great great grandson of Timothy naming his son, Michael John Jeffress Willis b.12.3.1992) Jonathon and Emily cared for his father at "Rookwood" during th
2 CONC e latter years of Timothy's life and until his death in 1888. Jonathon died of natural decay on 15 December 1934 at the age of 71 years and was buried in the Church of England Cemetery at Bowral. Emily died of double pneumonia at 
2 CONC Croydon on 11 June, 1941, aged 77 years and she was also buried in the Church of England Cemetery at Bowral
2 CONT
