2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 12 OCT 1800
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mayfield
3 POST TN20
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 OCT 1891
2 PLAC Benalla, Victoria, Australia
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Convict, arrived 1825
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Newnham-158
2 CONT
2 CONT > 1825: Philadelphia (again using the name Vinall) was again in the Lent Assizes, this time charged with receiving stolen goods [35]. She was found guilty and convicted to 1 year imprisonment. In the same court sessions, Philadelp
2 CONC hia's son Jonathan Harris was also found guilty of buglary and convicted to transportation for life to Australia. There is a note on Jonathan's record that "Philadelphia possibly let off for giving kings evidence in Jonothan's cas
2 CONC e". <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >One additional piece of evidence that strongly supports the conclusion that the three Philadelphia's (the wife of Thomas Allchorne; the partner of John Harris; and the wife of Alexander Vinall) are the same person, is a note on t
2 CONC he 1843 Tasmanian convict details for her son Jonathan Harris [39]. This includes a statement: "Remarks: Father: Jonathan at native place; 7 [sic] brothers: Thomas, George, John, Martin, Edward; 1 sister: Mary at native place.". T
2 CONC he first three brothers are Jonathan's older Allchorne half-siblings. The last two brothers are Jonathan's younger Vinall half-siblings (though interestingly Alexander is missing).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT **35.  Ancestry.com. England & Wales, Criminal Registers, 1791-1892. Original data: Home Office: Criminal Registers, Middlesex and Home Office: Criminal Registers, England and Wales; Source Citation: Class: HO 27; Piece: 30; Page:
2 CONC  204. See http://search.ancestry.com.au/cgi-bin/sse.dll?indiv=1&db=CriminalRegisters&h=1096212
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =links=
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/200260194/jonathan-harris
