1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''"The Cumberland Argus and Fruitgrowers Advocate", Thursday 15 July 1937'''
2 CONT KICK FROM HORSE BROUGHT DEATH TO NOTED TRAINER
2 CONT PASSING OF FRED MOORE
2 CONT
2 CONT Renowned in turf circles tlhroughout the State as a veteran rider and horse-trainer, Mr. Fred Moore, of Cabramatta, died in St. Vincent's Hospital on Monday as the result of a kick from a horse a fortnight previously.
2 CONT Mr. Moore, who commenced his career as a jockey, later went in for training horses at Warwick Farm, having taken up residence in Cabramatta 30 years ago. He was famous both as a hurdle rider, and a flat rider, and rode may steeds 
2 CONC to victory. His house, "Nimrod," Bloomfield-street, Cabramatta, was named after one of his best hurdlers.
2 CONT The interment took place in the Liver pool Church of England Cemetery. Mr. Moore is survived by a widow and a daughter, Freda.
