1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Colin James Tickner was born on the 6th Jnauary 1943 at the Royal Hospital for Women at Paddington. According to his death transcipt, he was dead several weeks prior to birth, therefore he was a stillborn baby. His
2 CONC  father was William Edward Tickner who was a labourer at the time. His mother was Lina Mary Tickner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Colin James Tickner was incinerated at the Royal Hospital for Women Paddington. The undertaker was Roy H. Syred who was also the medical attendant and the witnesses were R. D. Nunn & S. Whittingham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The informant was G. A. Newsham (registrar) of the Benevolent Society of NSW Sydney.
2 CONT
2 CONT His death was registered on the 19th January 1943 at Paddington. (Death Certificate Reference Number 1943/4766 NSW Family History Transcription Services PTY LTD).
2 CONT
2 CONT According to my mum (Colin's youngest sister), Lina Mary Tickner was told that she should not have any other children as she would not be able to carry them to term. Luckily, she went against the doctor's advice and she had 3 heal
2 CONC thy girls within the next 7 years.
