1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Colour Sergeant Samuel William Kilpatrick was born about 1782 at Lisburn County Antrim Northern Ireland. UK National Archives Depot Book WO25/448 1797-1800 records Samuel Kilpatrick five feet nine, 18 years old fresh complexion,ro
2 CONC und visage,grey eyes,sandy hair,born Lisburn County Antrim,trade cotton spinner,former service with Antrim Militia enlisted 4th Feb 1800. Depot Book WO/25/449 1814-1816 records Samuel Kilpatrick five feet ten age on enlistment 20,
2 CONC  fresh complexion,brown eyes,sandy hair,round visage,born Lisburn Co Antrim, attested at Belfast in Feb 1800 for unlimited service in West Undies 16th January 1801 to 1st June 1813, promoted to sergeant 5th September 1806. HMS Cey
2 CONC lon leaves Halifax Nova Scotis 25th May 1815 arrives Ostend 30th June 1815 with Wife Bridget and sons Samuel and William. WO97/776 Discharge Document states discharged Chatham Invalid Depot 24 Sept 1817 wife Bridget and two childr
2 CONC en has imperfect vision and dyspnoea. Pension Records WO120/27 1806-1838 Samuel age 40 receives pension 1 shilling and 11pence per day from 25 Sept 1817. ADM37/5242
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
