1 NAME Annie /Burges/
2 GIVN Annie
2 SURN Burges
2 _MARNM Burgess
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Kerang, Vic.
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1853
2 PLAC Long Gully, Bendigo
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1932
2 PLAC Hawthorn, Vic.
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Annie was born on the Bendigo goldfields at Long Gully in 1853.  When 18 years old, she married John Roberts, a 30 year old miner working at the Frederick the Great mine at Sebastian. After their marriage, they lived at Sebastian 
2 CONC where her husband worked as a mine manager.  
2 CONT Their first 3 children - Robert (1872), John (1874) and Margaret (1876) - were born there.  When Annie's mother died in 1874, her father and brothers, Charles and John moved in with them.  
2 CONT About 1879 Annie and John moved to Elmore.  Eva Jane Elmore Roberts was born there in that year.
2 CONT By 1880, with Annie's brothers, they moved to a farm at Durham Ox.  It was here that her crippled brother, John died in 1880.  Annie's eldest daughter, Margaret also died on the farm in 1885, aged only 9.
2 CONT Sometime later the family moved to a farm at Yassam, now known as Beauchamp (near Lake Boga and Swan Hill).
2 CONT Bonnie Roberts (Morvell) described her childhood memory of her Grandmother, Annie as follows -
2 CONT "I remember she was a petite lady.  (She) wore long black dresses to the floor and she wore 'little' bonnets tied under her chin (black of course) and a little black bag.  She was a stern lady, not very demonstrative toward me." 
2 CONT After death of her husband, Annie lived with her youngest daughter, Dorothy at Manning Tree Rd, Hawthorn, Melbourne.
